---
title: "release (LegionLinearEpochVesting)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_guardToken: onlyAskToken(token)
    q_guardToken --> q_guardCliff: onlyCliffEnded
    q_guardCliff --> q_checkCliff: block.timestamp >= cliffEndTimestamp?
    q_checkCliff --> q_revert: cliff not ended - revert CliffNotEnded
    q_checkCliff --> q_getCurrentEpoch: currentEpoch = getCurrentEpoch()
    q_getCurrentEpoch --> q_checkEpoch: currentEpoch > lastClaimedEpoch?
    q_checkEpoch --> q_noNewEpoch: no new epoch - standard linear release
    q_checkEpoch --> q_updateEpoch: _updateLastClaimedEpoch()
    q_updateEpoch --> q_calcVested: vestedAmount = _vestingSchedule(totalAllocation, timestamp)
    q_noNewEpoch --> q_calcVested: vestedAmount = _vestingSchedule(totalAllocation, timestamp)
    q_calcVested --> q_calcReleasable: releasable = vestedAmount - alreadyReleased
    q_calcReleasable --> q_transfer: safeTransfer(beneficiary, releasable)
    q_transfer --> q_emit: emit ERC20Released(token, releasable)
    q_emit --> [*]: return
    q_revert --> [*]: revert

    note right of q_guardToken
        INV-001: Only the designated askToken can be released
        INV-002: Prevents releasing other tokens accidentally sent to contract
    end note

    note right of q_getCurrentEpoch
        INV-003: Epoch-based linear vesting - releases at epoch boundaries
        INV-004: _vestingSchedule accounts for epoch granularity
        INV-005: currentEpoch = min((timestamp - start) / epochDuration, numberOfEpochs)
    end note
